WEBVTT

00:00:26.550 --> 00:00:27.780
<i>He pushed me...</i>

00:00:28.140 --> 00:00:29.490
<i>But why, Hayato?</i>

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:32.770
<i>There's no way I'll be able to climb this.</i>

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:38.140
<i>I'm gonna die...</i>

00:00:39.170 --> 00:00:40.690
<i>This is how it ends for me.</i>

00:00:42.400 --> 00:00:43.520
Oho.

00:00:44.230 --> 00:00:46.350
You're still alive.

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.940
It appears as though your 
companion pushed you.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:55.020
You climbed all the way up here 
with someone so treacherous.

00:00:55.020 --> 00:00:57.220
You must not be very smart.

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:01.100
<i>As I lay there dying...</i>

00:01:01.740 --> 00:01:03.620
<i>I saw a white illusion.</i>

00:02:15.990 --> 00:02:20.380
I have no idea why he'd push me. 
He was a trusted friend.

00:02:20.380 --> 00:02:23.580
You can't possibly be saying that right now.

00:02:24.800 --> 00:02:26.370
What are you?

00:02:26.370 --> 00:02:29.440
You're far too mean to be the 
last illusion I see before I die.

00:02:30.510 --> 00:02:34.830
Honestly... I even took on the form 
your kind seems familiar with.

00:02:34.830 --> 00:02:38.130
Do humans nowadays not 
know what a Yuki-Onna is?

00:02:40.130 --> 00:02:44.200
I mean... I always figured 
Yuki-Onna were more beautiful.

00:02:44.200 --> 00:02:48.070
Hey! You have some nerve saying 
that in the situation you're in!

00:02:48.070 --> 00:02:49.800
What does it matter?

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.310
Leave me here and I'll 
eventually freeze to death.

00:02:52.810 --> 00:02:56.840
So what difference would it 
make if a Yuki-Onna killed me?

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:01.130
It hasn't even crossed your 
mind to ask for my help?

00:03:01.130 --> 00:03:03.280
Well, Yuki-Onna kill humans, don't they?

00:03:03.870 --> 00:03:04.830
Tell me...

00:03:04.830 --> 00:03:08.720
Have you never read <i>Yuki-Onna</i> 
by Koizumi Yakumo?

00:03:09.090 --> 00:03:12.880
The young man in that tale 
was saved by a Yuki-Onna.

00:03:13.410 --> 00:03:17.050
On the other hand, what's a Yuki-Onna 
doing reading anything by Koizumi Yakumo?

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:20.060
Yuki-Onna are known to take on human form

00:03:20.060 --> 00:03:22.210
and mingle among them every now and then.

00:03:22.210 --> 00:03:25.510
Koizumi Yakumo wrote about that, as well.

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:38.150
This should get you through the night.

00:03:40.080 --> 00:03:43.220
It'd likely cause a commotion 
if the one who took a tumble

00:03:43.220 --> 00:03:46.680
were to show up at the foot of 
the mountain before the day is done.

00:03:46.680 --> 00:03:49.280
I shall escort you around evenfall tomorrow,

00:03:49.280 --> 00:03:51.020
so rest a while for now.

00:03:51.370 --> 00:03:53.090
Why are you helping me?

00:03:54.210 --> 00:03:58.410
Well... You're young, and...

00:04:00.030 --> 00:04:01.880
rather beautiful.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:04.800
That was a joke.

00:04:04.800 --> 00:04:09.410
You have fine features, 
but look at that scowl.

00:04:09.410 --> 00:04:10.600
You look a bit stern.

00:04:11.270 --> 00:04:13.440
If you manage to get 
down the mountain safely,

00:04:13.440 --> 00:04:15.190
you should read some of 
Koizumi Yakumo's works.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:17.630
Any time someone goes missing,

00:04:17.630 --> 00:04:19.820
the search efforts cause a 
commotion in these mountains.

00:04:20.110 --> 00:04:21.060
And sometimes,

00:04:21.060 --> 00:04:24.950
they even try to renovate the mountains 
to prevent further incidents.

00:04:24.950 --> 00:04:27.030
Meaning I'm better off saving you myself.

00:04:28.700 --> 00:04:31.540
By the way, do you have any money?

00:04:31.540 --> 00:04:33.870
Yeah, a decent amount.

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:36.480
Then give me half of that.

00:04:36.480 --> 00:04:37.900
If you have no money at all,

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:41.670
you'll have a rough time once you 
get back down, so I'll spare you.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:44.510
Not a bad price for saving your life, eh?

00:04:44.830 --> 00:04:47.080
What's a yokai going to do with money?

00:04:47.510 --> 00:04:51.360
The food and liquor you humans 
make as of late are quite tasty.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:54.060
But you cannot acquire 
them without money.

00:04:54.400 --> 00:04:57.560
I have the ability to take what 
I want without being seen...

00:04:57.560 --> 00:04:59.570
But then the shops would go under.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:02.940
If I carelessly wreaked 
havoc in your world,

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:05.180
I'd just be digging my own grave.

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:07.280
I must respect this rule.

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:11.030
But asking for a little bit 
in cases like this can't hurt.

00:05:11.470 --> 00:05:14.040
<i>She's actually respectable... for a yokai.</i>

00:05:14.510 --> 00:05:18.290
The thought of killing me and taking 
all of my money didn't cross your mind?

00:05:18.530 --> 00:05:21.290
Would you like me to change 
my mind and do that right now?

00:05:25.720 --> 00:05:27.190
No...

00:05:27.190 --> 00:05:27.930
In that case...

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:32.310
You're probably ready to apologize 
for saying that I'm not beautiful.

00:05:32.770 --> 00:05:37.440
The Yuki-Onna from the story is 
far more charming and refined.

00:05:38.990 --> 00:05:42.560
I thought about killing you if you 
gave me an empty compliment...

00:05:43.010 --> 00:05:45.140
But I guess you didn't fall for that.

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:48.700
Hey, don't try setting any weird traps now.

00:05:48.700 --> 00:05:52.410
I'm joking. Survive until the morn.

00:05:52.920 --> 00:05:56.380
I'm not going to feel responsible 
if you freeze to death.

00:06:01.810 --> 00:06:03.750
It wasn't an illusion?

00:06:05.030 --> 00:06:07.010
I... survived?

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:19.690
Hello!

00:06:21.920 --> 00:06:24.360
Ah, so you survived.

00:06:24.360 --> 00:06:26.510
Ow! Ow, ow, ow...

00:06:26.510 --> 00:06:28.570
What? Where does it hurt?

00:06:28.570 --> 00:06:29.780
Everywhere.

00:06:30.710 --> 00:06:33.370
All right... How's this?

00:06:36.480 --> 00:06:37.960
Don't fall.

00:06:37.960 --> 00:06:39.460
Down the mountain we go!

00:06:54.960 --> 00:06:56.230
<i>Wow...</i>

00:06:56.540 --> 00:07:00.310
I'm sure I don't need to tell you this, 
but do not tell your parents, siblings,

00:07:00.310 --> 00:07:02.380
wife, or children about me.

00:07:02.380 --> 00:07:07.360
If you tell even a single soul, I will come 
to kill you, no matter where you are.

00:07:08.960 --> 00:07:12.870
So if I ever want to die, I just 
need to tell someone about you.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:16.820
Your life is being saved here. 
Stop talking as though your future is grim.

00:07:16.820 --> 00:07:17.750
I'm kidding.

00:07:18.070 --> 00:07:19.430
I'll keep this secret.

00:07:20.970 --> 00:07:25.180
Not that anyone would believe me if I told 
them I was saved by a Yuki-Onna, anyway.

00:07:27.580 --> 00:07:30.590
Masayuki fell head-first off 
a ridge near the summit.

00:07:31.070 --> 00:07:33.790
He fell into a pile of snow, 
and I couldn't see him anymore.

00:07:34.590 --> 00:07:36.930
I should've gone back 
and searched for him.

00:07:37.390 --> 00:07:39.390
Now, don't go blaming yourself for this.

00:07:39.390 --> 00:07:42.090
We'll send out a search 
party tomorrow morning.

00:07:48.960 --> 00:07:50.570
M-Masayuki?!

00:07:50.990 --> 00:07:53.310
Why... How are you alive?

00:07:54.710 --> 00:07:56.500
He pushed me off the ledge.

00:07:58.200 --> 00:08:00.020
I was sure I was going to die,

00:08:00.020 --> 00:08:02.130
but I miraculously found 
a path down the mountain,

00:08:02.130 --> 00:08:03.210
and managed to survive.

00:08:03.540 --> 00:08:05.370
Please apprehend him immediately.

00:08:08.300 --> 00:08:10.090
We got testimony from the suspect.

00:08:10.420 --> 00:08:12.230
He said he just couldn't help himself.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:16.460
A woman he was in love 
with had a crush on you,

00:08:16.460 --> 00:08:19.600
and she had asked him to help 
her with asking you out.

00:08:20.110 --> 00:08:23.100
He was jealous of you, but he 
wanted the best for the woman.

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:25.010
Yet when he talked to you...

00:08:26.400 --> 00:08:27.820
Who's that?

00:08:29.250 --> 00:08:33.260
The fact that you had no interest 
whatsoever pushed him over the edge.

00:08:33.850 --> 00:08:38.210
If you were to die and he got close to 
the woman while she was grieving,

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:40.540
he thought he could then make her his.

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:45.040
Those were the thoughts 
that crossed his mind.

00:08:46.530 --> 00:08:48.420
Well, that's a pathetic reason.

00:08:48.800 --> 00:08:50.150
It's hard to believe

00:08:50.150 --> 00:08:54.400
that's the reason my friend 
from high school tried to kill me...

00:08:54.790 --> 00:08:55.550
No...

00:08:56.240 --> 00:08:59.810
Perhaps I'm the only one 
who considered us friends.

00:08:59.810 --> 00:09:04.020
<b>The Complete Works of Koizumi Yakumo</b>

00:09:06.140 --> 00:09:10.650
Hayato's parents would like you to 
accept monetary compensation.

00:09:10.910 --> 00:09:14.610
They seemed to have no intention 
of backing down from this offer.

00:09:15.820 --> 00:09:19.030
Their family is quite wealthy. 
If you want this to be over with quickly,

00:09:19.030 --> 00:09:21.610
you're better off just accepting their offer.

00:09:21.930 --> 00:09:24.960
All right. I'll let you 
handle the trial, as well.

00:09:25.590 --> 00:09:28.830
It'll just be awkward if I ever 
have to see Hayato again.

00:09:28.830 --> 00:09:30.660
I'd prefer not to see him.

00:09:33.480 --> 00:09:36.840
There are truly terrifying 
things in this world.

00:09:34.650 --> 00:09:36.840
<b>The Complete Works of Koizumi Yakumo</b>

00:09:39.630 --> 00:09:41.810
I'm never going mountain-climbing again.

00:09:45.700 --> 00:09:47.810
<b>Eleven Years Later</b>

00:10:16.920 --> 00:10:18.880
<i>Ah, I see...</i>

00:10:18.880 --> 00:10:22.890
Honestly... I even took on the form 
your kind seems familiar with.

00:10:22.890 --> 00:10:24.650
<i>So that's what's going on.</i>

00:10:31.200 --> 00:10:34.130
Long ago, as I lay dying in the mountains,

00:10:34.450 --> 00:10:37.690
I met a woman who thought 
of herself as quite a beauty.

00:10:36.440 --> 00:10:40.320
Hand-crafted
Soba

00:10:40.770 --> 00:10:45.500
She called herself "Yuki-Onna" and 
saved me with her ayakashi powers.

00:10:58.690 --> 00:11:01.050
And thanks to that, I'm alive today...

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:04.220
But sometimes I can't help 
wondering if that was

00:11:04.220 --> 00:11:06.470
actually a dream or reality.

00:11:08.650 --> 00:11:10.020
Wait, wait, wait!

00:11:10.020 --> 00:11:13.700
Did I not say that I would 
kill you if you told anyone?!

00:11:13.700 --> 00:11:16.520
I was just reminiscing with 
someone else who was there.

00:11:17.020 --> 00:11:19.940
You still haven't read 
Koizumi Yakumo's story?

00:11:19.940 --> 00:11:25.410
The Yuki-Onna was furious with the man 
in that story when he broke his promise.

00:11:25.720 --> 00:11:27.050
I read it.

00:11:27.050 --> 00:11:31.690
In that story, the man told his wife, 
not realizing that she was the Yuki-Onna.

00:11:32.170 --> 00:11:34.820
But I'm telling you all of 
this knowing very well

00:11:34.820 --> 00:11:36.670
that you are the Yuki-Onna from back then,

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:38.890
so it doesn't count as telling anyone else.

00:11:38.890 --> 00:11:41.710
Isn't that what you call sophistry?

00:11:42.090 --> 00:11:43.130
Be that as it may,

00:11:43.130 --> 00:11:46.910
I'm surprised you could tell I was 
that Yuki-Onna from your past.

00:11:47.710 --> 00:11:51.100
Your face and pale skin are the same. 
I wouldn't mistake you for anyone.

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:57.120
Ah, I guess I can't hide my beauty.

00:11:57.120 --> 00:11:59.060
It's nothing to brag about.

00:11:59.060 --> 00:12:02.840
Would you like me to drag you back 
to the place where you lay dying?

00:12:03.400 --> 00:12:04.990
That wouldn't be so bad, actually.

00:12:06.350 --> 00:12:08.240
I'm surprised you recognized me, as well.

00:12:08.630 --> 00:12:13.660
It's been over ten years. 
I'm sure my face has changed with age.

00:12:14.070 --> 00:12:17.910
You're the only human I 
remember saving recently.

00:12:17.910 --> 00:12:23.710
Besides, we ayakashi don't just distinguish 
you humans by physical appearances.

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:21.920
Soft
Serve

00:12:23.710 --> 00:12:27.720
Each of you has a presence and color 
that does not change so easily.

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:28.970
Huh...

00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:35.680
Soft Serve

00:12:30.990 --> 00:12:34.710
I always felt bad that I never 
got to return the favor.

00:12:34.710 --> 00:12:37.670
I'm a working adult now with 
a little more money to spare.

00:12:38.170 --> 00:12:41.500
I can buy you a few dozen orders 
of soft serve if you'd like.

00:12:41.500 --> 00:12:44.150
I don't really need a few dozen of these, but...

00:12:44.450 --> 00:12:47.830
It <i>is</i> difficult for me to acquire 
human money these days,

00:12:47.830 --> 00:12:49.910
and prices on everything have gone up.

00:12:49.910 --> 00:12:53.160
I still get nervous going into human shops.

00:12:53.160 --> 00:12:56.840
They yammer on about point cards 
and days with special deals...

00:12:56.840 --> 00:12:59.960
I know nothing of your calendar, 
so it all confuses me.

00:13:00.220 --> 00:13:03.730
Though if you were to go in with me, 
I could pick out what I want at leisure,

00:13:03.730 --> 00:13:05.320
and I wouldn't get confused.

00:13:05.320 --> 00:13:08.590
I started renting a house on
the outskirts of town this month.

00:13:09.040 --> 00:13:12.140
It's a perfect place for you 
to eat in peace, as well.

00:13:12.140 --> 00:13:14.860
Ah! Does that mean you can cook?

00:13:14.860 --> 00:13:17.680
They do say some dishes taste 
best right after they're made.

00:13:17.960 --> 00:13:22.190
Yeah. I learned how to cook 
after my divorce last year.

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:27.400
Now that I get a closer look, 
you do seem rather pale.

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:29.650
I have a strong mistrust of other people.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:33.250
My wife, whom I trusted deeply, had a lover,

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:35.560
and I was almost killed yet again.

00:13:35.560 --> 00:13:37.160
In the end, we divorced.

00:13:37.610 --> 00:13:39.490
This happened last June.

00:13:39.490 --> 00:13:42.280
Also, the company I started 
right out of college

00:13:42.280 --> 00:13:46.800
was swallowed up by a bigger company three 
months ago due to a colleague's betrayal.

00:13:47.370 --> 00:13:49.940
As the president, of course, 
there was no place left for me there.

00:13:49.940 --> 00:13:53.670
I was betrayed by my friend, my wife, 
and my colleague, and then I lost my job.

00:13:53.670 --> 00:13:55.720
I can't trust people at all now.

00:13:56.610 --> 00:13:59.230
I felt like there was no one 
else I could talk to

00:13:59.230 --> 00:14:01.680
except a yokai.

00:14:03.570 --> 00:14:07.600
That's why I got my affairs in order 
as much as possible and moved here.

00:14:08.090 --> 00:14:10.950
I never expected to just happen 
to run into you here, though.

00:14:11.270 --> 00:14:14.450
That means you're probably just 
barely getting by, doesn't it?

00:14:14.450 --> 00:14:16.560
You won't get the best of me.

00:14:16.560 --> 00:14:19.330
<i>I see she's as sensible as ever.</i>

00:14:19.690 --> 00:14:23.960
I lost my position as president, but that 
doesn't mean I lost my personal fortune.

00:14:24.490 --> 00:14:27.420
I have enough money to live comfortably 
for the next thirty years or so.

00:14:29.070 --> 00:14:30.630
You should've told me that first!

00:14:30.630 --> 00:14:33.510
That means you're plenty blessed.

00:14:33.510 --> 00:14:36.950
Not to mention, you survived 
almost getting killed twice,

00:14:36.950 --> 00:14:39.080
so you must be rather lucky.

00:14:39.080 --> 00:14:41.940
Men who have money and can't trust others

00:14:41.940 --> 00:14:45.770
are always the bad guys who 
end up punished in folktales.

00:14:46.100 --> 00:14:47.900
You're so pitiful.

00:14:49.100 --> 00:14:52.650
I'd like some fine liquor. And I want 
to eat some fish from the sea.

00:14:53.150 --> 00:14:56.660
If I can make that a part of this deal, 
I wouldn't mind lending you an ear.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:14:59.380
I'm about to go grocery shopping.

00:14:59.380 --> 00:15:02.250
You can put whatever you want, 
as much as you want, in the cart.

00:15:02.700 --> 00:15:05.260
If there's any dish you'd like 
to eat, I'll cook it for you.

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:15.010
<i>Yuki-Onna then started coming over 
at night, two or three times a week.</i>

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:19.840
Masayuki! Take me to the grocery store today!

00:15:21.520 --> 00:15:24.480
I want to pick just the right ingredients!

00:15:24.780 --> 00:15:28.310
In that case, let's head to a bigger 
commercial facility outside of town.

00:15:28.310 --> 00:15:32.270
If I keep taking you around town here, 
they'll start to remember your face.

00:15:34.780 --> 00:15:38.030
A car? Wow! I've never been in one before!

00:15:42.540 --> 00:15:44.410
<b>Low Prices Every Day!</b>

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.710
Saury

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.710
Our Top Pick

00:15:45.290 --> 00:15:46.710
Black
Sea Bream

00:15:56.010 --> 00:15:57.430
Shrimp Gratin

00:16:08.070 --> 00:16:11.070
Ginjo sake is the best kind of sake!

00:16:11.070 --> 00:16:13.570
Beer is great, too, but I prefer happoshu.

00:16:14.830 --> 00:16:16.030
Hey...

00:16:16.030 --> 00:16:18.200
Are you sure you're okay 
with just curry udon?

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:22.110
That's fine. In fact, that's 
specifically what I want to eat.

00:16:22.110 --> 00:16:23.370
That's pretty cheap.

00:16:23.370 --> 00:16:26.420
I don't know what ingredients 
are expensive or cheap.

00:16:26.870 --> 00:16:30.210
But you probably shouldn't 
eat this with that kimono on.

00:16:30.480 --> 00:16:32.960
Eating curry udon in white clothes is taboo.

00:16:33.420 --> 00:16:37.180
What are you talking about? 
This is what a Yuki-Onna should look like.

00:16:41.910 --> 00:16:43.070
It's delicious!

00:16:43.070 --> 00:16:45.820
This roux is different from 
the one you use for rice!

00:16:45.820 --> 00:16:48.190
Why isn't it getting on your clothes?

00:16:49.210 --> 00:16:50.940
<b>Four
Months
Later</b>

00:16:50.130 --> 00:16:50.940
Right now?

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:52.890
I'm home alone.

00:16:52.890 --> 00:16:54.800
I've just been a shut-in, as usual.

00:16:54.800 --> 00:16:55.860
<i>I see.</i>

00:16:56.340 --> 00:16:59.680
I'm planning on having a drink 
and reading until dawn.

00:17:00.110 --> 00:17:00.990
<i>President...</i>

00:17:01.480 --> 00:17:02.830
I'm not the president anymore.

00:17:03.270 --> 00:17:06.600
<i>Please excuse me. Muroi-san...</i>

00:17:06.600 --> 00:17:07.330
What is it?

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:11.670
<i>I'll be waiting for you to start a new job.</i>

00:17:12.010 --> 00:17:12.730
Right...

00:17:13.070 --> 00:17:15.770
Well, I'm gonna hang up. 
I'll leave the rest to you.

00:17:15.770 --> 00:17:17.340
<i>Right. Goodnight.</i>

00:17:21.270 --> 00:17:24.060
This warmth when it's freshly 
fried is irresistible!

00:17:24.590 --> 00:17:27.430
I prefer eating this with 
salt rather than the sauce.

00:17:27.430 --> 00:17:29.770
A Yuki-Onna who likes heat...

00:17:30.510 --> 00:17:34.130
In folktales, they say your kind 
melted from the fire in hearths,

00:17:34.130 --> 00:17:35.190
or from hot tea.

00:17:35.520 --> 00:17:37.510
Your body's not affected?

00:17:37.510 --> 00:17:39.420
When are these folktales from?

00:17:39.420 --> 00:17:43.000
If that was all it took, 
a Yuki-Onna wouldn't survive a year.

00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:46.630
People say and believe that 
Yuki-Onna mixed with humans

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:48.330
and produced many children.

00:17:48.330 --> 00:17:51.160
I'll be damned if I melt 
just from eating tempura.

00:17:51.160 --> 00:17:52.830
I have a question...

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:59.700
Are there other yokai like yourself that 
have blended into our society unnoticed?

00:17:59.700 --> 00:18:01.270
I'm sure there are.

00:18:01.270 --> 00:18:04.970
But getting involved with humans 
in any way can lead to trouble,

00:18:04.970 --> 00:18:07.180
so most keep their distance.

00:18:07.670 --> 00:18:10.960
Not all supernatural beings 
are stronger than humans,

00:18:10.960 --> 00:18:13.810
and it's more peaceful if both 
sides leave each other alone.

00:18:14.310 --> 00:18:19.560
Since humans don't fear or respect how 
the world is, they are quite dangerous.

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:24.990
But you coming here to visit 
me doesn't cause any issues?

00:18:24.990 --> 00:18:29.120
Some of my kind have warned me to stay away.

00:18:29.120 --> 00:18:31.580
Though some say it might be better to have

00:18:31.580 --> 00:18:34.420
one of us stay close to 
learn more about humans.

00:18:36.690 --> 00:18:42.690
Though I have asked our lady if I am 
taking advantage of you too much.

00:18:42.690 --> 00:18:43.890
"Lady"?

00:18:43.890 --> 00:18:44.680
Yes.

00:18:44.680 --> 00:18:47.270
She is the goddess of wisdom to those of us

00:18:47.270 --> 00:18:51.100
who call ourselves ayakashi, 
yokai, ghosts, and demons.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:54.470
Of course, our kind have disputes, as well,

00:18:54.470 --> 00:18:57.920
and sometimes, we cannot solve 
those problems on our own.

00:18:57.920 --> 00:19:01.950
There are also those who are troubled 
by what humans do and seek resolutions.

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:06.210
Those are the times when 
we rely on our lady.

00:19:07.610 --> 00:19:09.890
I've only had the honor of meeting her twice,

00:19:09.890 --> 00:19:14.490
but I am in awe at her accomplishments 
and how wise she is.

00:19:14.490 --> 00:19:19.040
So she's someone you yokai consider a god... 
She must be a special kind of monster.

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:22.150
No, our lady is a human.

00:19:24.560 --> 00:19:26.940
She stands between humans and the ayakashi,

00:19:26.940 --> 00:19:30.470
and is tasked with maintaining 
order in the world.

00:19:31.110 --> 00:19:33.880
Her human perspective is vital to us.

00:19:33.880 --> 00:19:37.980
It was us who made that 
human into a goddess.

00:19:39.070 --> 00:19:43.150
So what did your lady say about 
you spending time with me?

00:19:43.150 --> 00:19:47.510
She said she did not mind, as long as 
I kept out of sight of other humans

00:19:47.510 --> 00:19:49.410
and was careful not to let 
you take advantage of me.

00:19:49.780 --> 00:19:51.930
We can help out humanity 
every once in a while,

00:19:51.930 --> 00:19:56.770
but she said we must not let our powers 
influence the world of man too much.

00:19:56.770 --> 00:20:00.170
Well said. Sounds like she has 
a good head on her shoulders.

00:20:00.400 --> 00:20:04.790
She also said that if any trouble arises, 
I should freeze you to death and flee.

00:20:04.790 --> 00:20:08.350
That's an awfully violent solution, lady.

00:20:11.630 --> 00:20:15.100
By the way, how are things 
going with your neighbors?

00:20:15.450 --> 00:20:18.350
Well, I am a shut-in from out 
of town with a scary face.

00:20:18.350 --> 00:20:22.050
My neighbors are scared 
of me, so they avoid me.

00:20:22.050 --> 00:20:24.350
I don't think they see me as an 
upstanding member of society.

00:20:25.850 --> 00:20:28.850
Since I never see anyone, I may 
have forgotten how to speak

00:20:28.850 --> 00:20:31.240
If I didn't have you around.

00:20:31.240 --> 00:20:35.820
Oh, please. You just had 
a phone call earlier.

00:20:36.470 --> 00:20:39.210
One of my former subordinates 
was just keeping me in the loop.

00:20:39.440 --> 00:20:42.300
Are you sure she doesn't miss your talent?

00:20:42.610 --> 00:20:44.880
Yeah, well, she's the only one.

00:20:44.880 --> 00:20:48.180
Even a single ally would prove 
useful if you were to start over.

00:20:48.180 --> 00:20:52.360
Plus, you look far livelier 
now than you did before.

00:20:52.360 --> 00:20:56.800
And I don't mind keeping you company 
until your spirits lift a bit.

00:20:57.980 --> 00:21:02.590
I'm pretty content, thanks to all 
the delicious foods I get to eat...

00:21:02.590 --> 00:21:06.120
Hm... Perhaps I'm benefiting 
too much from this.

00:21:06.650 --> 00:21:07.610
I know!

00:21:07.880 --> 00:21:11.120
It has been some time since you 
left your former wife, has it not?

00:21:11.120 --> 00:21:14.200
If you'd like, I could keep you
company at night, as well.

00:21:17.360 --> 00:21:20.400
Do yokai lack any kind of morals?

00:21:20.400 --> 00:21:22.760
Besides, if I had to rely 
on you to <i>that</i> extent,

00:21:22.760 --> 00:21:24.790
then I'd truly be pathetic.

00:21:25.260 --> 00:21:28.260
As they say, "Shameful is he who 
spurns a woman's invitation."

00:21:28.260 --> 00:21:30.760
Ah, or are you an ass man?

00:21:30.760 --> 00:21:33.530
Could you please let me retain 
a little bit of dignity here?

00:21:33.920 --> 00:21:36.270
I'm no different from a 
dead person right now.

00:21:36.270 --> 00:21:38.280
I'm not fit to be with you.

00:21:38.880 --> 00:21:43.420
Besides, I don't think your lady would 
allow our relations to go that far.

00:21:43.420 --> 00:21:46.440
She said she was fine with it, 
as long as we use contraceptives.

00:21:48.230 --> 00:21:51.370
Maybe we can't trust this lady after all...

00:21:53.620 --> 00:21:55.580
<b>Sep.</b>

00:21:55.910 --> 00:21:59.810
Ooh! Maybe that's the 
hitsumabushi we ordered!

00:22:00.520 --> 00:22:02.000
Hey, Masayuki!

00:22:02.000 --> 00:22:04.830
I'll watch this! Go and answer the door!

00:22:04.830 --> 00:22:07.280
They'll have to redeliver it if you don't!

00:22:07.280 --> 00:22:08.200
Right.

00:22:08.910 --> 00:22:09.890
Coming.

00:22:12.150 --> 00:22:14.270
You must be Muroi Masayuki-san.

00:22:14.270 --> 00:22:15.430
Yes...

00:22:18.530 --> 00:22:20.270
Are you aware that

00:22:20.270 --> 00:22:24.630
Harada Miharu-san, the woman you 
divorced last year, has been murdered?

00:22:28.160 --> 00:22:29.360
Yikes...

00:22:30.230 --> 00:22:32.570
Is that your new client?

00:22:32.920 --> 00:22:35.170
This is actually my messenger.

00:22:35.170 --> 00:22:38.490
My client is actually a Yuki-Onna 
who lives up in the mountains.

00:22:38.870 --> 00:22:40.250
A Yuki-Onna?

00:22:40.250 --> 00:22:43.870
<b>A Woman's Body Found by the Riverbank</b>

00:22:40.500 --> 00:22:42.370
On the night of September 12th,

00:22:42.370 --> 00:22:46.980
a woman named Harada Miharu 
was found beaten to death,

00:22:46.980 --> 00:22:49.890
but none of the news sites 
have much information.

00:22:49.890 --> 00:22:51.380
Not many documents on it, either.

00:22:51.380 --> 00:22:55.450
So what does the Yuki-Onna have 
to do with this murder case?

00:22:55.450 --> 00:22:59.390
Well, the police have a 
prime suspect in this case.

00:22:59.750 --> 00:23:04.790
According to the Yuki-Onna, this person 
has an alibi and can't be the culprit.

00:23:04.790 --> 00:23:07.400
So she'd like us to help him out.

00:23:07.400 --> 00:23:10.650
He has an alibi, but he's the prime suspect?

00:23:10.960 --> 00:23:14.220
Well, the only one who can back 
up his alibi is this Yuki-Onna,

00:23:14.220 --> 00:23:16.620
so neither of them can 
mention her to the police.

00:23:18.550 --> 00:23:20.790
Why aren't you back yet, Masayuki?

00:23:21.090 --> 00:23:24.240
It'll burn if you don't come back soon!

00:23:26.920 --> 00:23:28.750
Hey, Masayu—

00:23:35.440 --> 00:23:36.930
Is something the matter?

00:23:36.930 --> 00:23:38.760
Er, no...

00:23:39.980 --> 00:23:40.930
Oh?

00:23:41.520 --> 00:23:43.100
You have a pet rabbit?

00:23:47.020 --> 00:23:50.020
To be continued
